ms</category> <category>computer-science</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Merge Sort&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;```rust fn mergeSort(s: Sequence) -&amp;gt; Sequence { if s.length() &amp;lt;= 1 { return s; }&lt;/p&gt; &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;let (left, right) = split(s); &lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt; &lt;p&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Algorithms/Merge%20Sort/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:10:26 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Algorithms/Merge%20Sort/</guid> </item> <item> <title>QuickSort</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;``` function quicksort(array, left, right) if right &amp;lt;= left return&lt;/p&gt; &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;pivotIndex = partition(array, left, right) quicksort(arr... &lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Algorithms/QuickSort/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:10:26 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Algorithms/QuickSort/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Caching</title> <category>computer-science</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Caching&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;Structurally, a &lt;a href=&#34;./Caching.md&#34;&gt;cache&lt;/a&gt; is organized into blocks of fixed size called &lt;strong&gt;cache blocks&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;cache lines&lt;/strong&gt;. Data can be transfer into...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Caching/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:10:26 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Caching/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Direct Mapped Cache</title> <category>computer-science</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Direct Mapped Cache&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;The entire address space consisting of $2^n$ addresses is split into $2^k$ blocks and each $n$-bit memory address is logically divided...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Direct%20Mapped%20Cache/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:10:26 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Direct%20Mapped%20Cache/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Fully Associative Cache</title> <category>computer-science</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Fully Associative Cache&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;In a &lt;strong&gt;fully associative cache&lt;/strong&gt; each $n$-bit memory address is split into a $k$-bit &lt;strong&gt;tag&lt;/strong&gt; and a $b$-bit &lt;strong&gt;offset&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;During rea...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Fully%20Associative%20Cache/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:10:26 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Fully%20Associative%20Cache/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Set Associative Cache</title> <category>computer-science</category> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Set Associative Cache&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;Set number chooses the set of cache lines to look through. Tag is then compared with all tags within the set to find data. Associat...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Caching/Set%20Associative%20Cache/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:10:26 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss